(The list field of a thing parameter passed on to a value parameter is a
 copy: freeing the field through a list parameter leaves the value whole.)
A thing called note has
  a list called items.

To 'look' with a value called kept and a list called items.
    Free items.
    Print "kept: {kept}".

To 'pass on' with a note called given.
    'look' of given's items and given's items.
    Print "given: {given's items}".

a note called memo.
append "a" to memo's items.
'pass on' of memo.
Print "memo: {memo's items}".
